WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.448
Okay, so you and I know each other,

2
00:00:02.448 --> 00:00:05.600
we've known each other over many years

3
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.440
in similar circles and circumstances.

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.300
We've really spoken to each other

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.456
like two women, two humans.

6
00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:17.710
And what I didn't know was that

7
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.056
you were staying at Anna Wintour's house,

8
00:00:21.056 --> 00:00:26.056
and that she was a source of consistent check-ins

9
00:00:27.816 --> 00:00:32.440
as well as encouragement for this.

10
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:33.273
Is this true?

11
00:00:33.273 --> 00:00:34.610
Absolutely true.

12
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.948
You know, the book was her idea.

13
00:00:36.948 --> 00:00:40.200
And to have a friend like Anna,

14
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.140
she really was the first person who called me

15
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.182
right after the 2016 election, and,

16
00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:48.940
when half the country was in mourning over that loss,

17
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.230
and I was so devastated, I was so shattered

18
00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.730
and she calls me and said, "We're going to dinner."

19
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.877
And at dinner, she said, "I know what you should do next.

20
00:00:55.877 --> 00:00:56.710
"You should write your story,

21
00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.880
"it's a good story and you should write it."

22
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.010
And I wasn't convinced that I would,

23
00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.990
I went and talked to Hillary a couple of days later,

24
00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:03.823
she said I should do it.

25
00:01:03.823 --> 00:01:06.010 line:15%
It took some convincing for me to do it, but I did,

26
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:06.890 line:15%
and I'm glad I did.

27
00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.860 line:15%
And it's been incredible therapy.

28
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.044 line:15%
And being out in the world,

29
00:01:10.044 --> 00:01:13.000 line:15%
there's something so liberating and empowering about it.

30
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:13.833
I really enjoyed it.

31
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:16.440
I'm so excited to know that like Anna Wintour

32
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.112
was there to nurture you.

33
00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:23.380
And she's not the warmest creature,

34
00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.380
so I love hearing that this very stoic woman was

35
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.400
what you needed when she was there for you.

36
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.730
Well, she actually gave me the gift of friendship

37
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.300
at a time when I really needed it.

38
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.390
It was in the midst of one of my very difficult periods

39
00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.230
in my marriage.

40
00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:47.230 line:15%
And there was a public demand that I be fired

41
00:01:47.877 --> 00:01:50.693 line:15%
because I had chosen to stay with my husband

42
00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.490
who had been unfaithful to me.

43
00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.840
And I, at that moment, had chosen to stay with him.

44
00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.400
And I remember we were at this dinner,

45
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.375
and all the headlines were, "Is Hillary gonna fire Huma?"

46
00:02:01.375 --> 00:02:04.380
And in the middle of this dinner, she walks over to me,

47
00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.887
as, you know, the cameras are following and says,

48
00:02:06.887 --> 00:02:08.295
"Would you like to have lunch some time?"

49
00:02:08.295 --> 00:02:13.295
And really ever since that moment, pushed me all the time,

50
00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.380
was always there if I needed something,

51
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.597
but pushed me to make decisions, to stay true to myself,

52
00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:20.460
to not listen to my detractors.

53
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.810
And I'm really great, I had that with Hillary

54
00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:22.643
and I've had that with Anna,

55
00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:25.000
and I'm just privileged to have two women like that

56
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:25.833
in my life.

57
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:28.050
All right, we're talking about really strong women,

58
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.030
huge figures here.

59
00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.616
And, Hillary, you know,

60
00:02:32.616 --> 00:02:35.565
HRC as you call her throughout the book.

61
00:02:35.565 --> 00:02:40.565
And she famously made a life choice, a political decision,

62
00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.160
a personal decision, and we're putting ourselves out there.

63
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.490
So make no mistake, we've chosen public life.

64
00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.390
Yes.

65
00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.760
We're not naive about that.

66
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.164
We've made a conscious choice.

67
00:02:50.164 --> 00:02:51.290
Yes.

68
00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.800
And is it true that you would go

69
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:58.170
and talk to her each time a transgression,

70
00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.760
as you call it throughout the book,

71
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.070
with Anthony, you would go into her office,

72
00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.500
a woman who probably there's no one

73
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.800
who could understand more living in the life,

74
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.320
being a huge political figure.

75
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.700
What were those conversations?

76
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.410
I think one of the greatest gifts,

77
00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:18.166
walking into the White House at 21

78
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:20.920
during the Clinton administration, I joined this club.

79
00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.890
It's a club that comes with lifetime membership

80
00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.510 line:15%
and it's a club called Hillaryland.

81
00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.740 line:15%
And the thing that's amazing about being

82
00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.770 line:15%
in this environment is that it was a workspace

83
00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.240 line:15%
where you walked in and you felt like you were respected

84
00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.520
and your work was valued,

85
00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:37.610
and everyone took responsibility for things as a community.

86
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.800
It was very much a sense of support.

87
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.670
So, I would say that it was a place

88
00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:45.430
where as women climbed up the ladders of success,

89
00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.210
they did not step on the fingers of the women below them,

90
00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.410
but reached the lowest and pull the rest of us up too.

91
00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.770
So it was an environment where I was like,

92
00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:54.980
how do we do this job better?

93
00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.410
Or you did a great job on that speech.

94
00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:57.539
How's your mother doing?

95
00:03:57.539 --> 00:03:59.580
You should go talk to my allergist.

96
00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.560
Happy birthday.

97
00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:01.393
Right.

98
00:04:01.393 --> 00:04:02.740
And Hillaryland was all of those things

99
00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:04.730
because Hillary Clinton is all of those things.

100
00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.430
And so, to be part of that community,

101
00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:09.200
I think did help me throughout

102
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.600
obviously the highs in my life

103
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.070
and certainly the lows in my life.

104
00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.570
And every time I did have a personal problem,

105
00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:16.020
and it wasn't just in my relationship,

106
00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.530
just generally, I'm not feeling well,

107
00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.219
my mom is not doing well,

108
00:04:19.219 --> 00:04:22.980
she always approached these conversations as a friend first

109
00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.550
and as a boss second.

110
00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.533
And the advice she always gave me was,

111
00:04:28.497 --> 00:04:31.470
"I'm here, you do what is right for you."

112
00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:32.923
It was never judgmental,

113
00:04:32.923 --> 00:04:36.595
"And whatever you choose to do, I'm gonna support you."

114
00:04:36.595 --> 00:04:39.262
(upbeat music)

